ALGORITHM CSP_SCHEDULING

1. Create variables E1, E2, E3, E4, E5, E6.
2. Assign possible time slots and halls to each exam.
3. Apply hall-capacity constraints.
4. Select the unassigned exam with the smallest domain using MRV.
5. Assign a valid time slot and hall.
6. Apply Forward Checking:
      Remove conflicting values from neighbouring exams.
7. If any domain becomes empty:
      Backtrack to the previous assignment.
8. Otherwise, select the next exam using MRV.
9. Repeat Steps 5–8 until all exams are assigned.
10. Return the valid examination timetable.
11. Stop.
